{"module":"Term 2","title":"Unit 6 — Health and Welfare","description":"Body and illnesses, healthy habits, should / must / have to, giving advice.","intro":"This unit deals with health problems, healthy lifestyles and advice.","objectifs":["Name common illnesses and symptoms.","Use should, must, have to, mustn’t, don’t have to.","Ask for and give advice."],"cours":[{"t":"Vocabulary","h":"<ul><li>a headache, a toothache, a cold, the flu, a fever, a cough, to sneeze</li><li>a prescription, a pharmacy, to get fit, to work out, stress, an addiction</li></ul>"},{"t":"Grammar: modals of advice and obligation","h":"<table><tr><th>Modal</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Example</th></tr><tr><td>should / shouldn’t</td><td>advice</td><td>You should drink more water.</td></tr><tr><td>must</td><td>strong obligation (speaker)</td><td>You must stop smoking.</td></tr><tr><td>have to</td><td>obligation (rule)</td><td>Students have to wear a uniform.</td></tr><tr><td>mustn’t</td><td>prohibition</td><td>You mustn’t take this without a prescription.</td></tr><tr><td>don’t have to</td><td>no obligation</td><td>You don’t have to come.</td></tr></table><div class=\"box note\"><span class=\"box-title\">Form</span><p>Modal + base verb (no “to”, no -s): <i>He <b>should see</b> a doctor.</i></p></div>"},{"t":"Communication","h":"<ul><li>Asking: “What should I do?” / “What do you advise me to do?”</li><li>Advising: “You’d better rest.” / “If I were you, I’d see a dentist.” / “Why don’t you…?”</li></ul>"}],"recap":"should = advice ; must / have to = obligation ; mustn’t = prohibition ; don’t have to = not necessary. Modal + base verb. Advice: You should… / If I were you, I’d… / Why don’t you…?","cards":[["should","Advice"],["mustn’t","Prohibition (it is forbidden)"],["don’t have to","Not necessary"],["If I were you…","…I would + verb (advice)"]],"exercises":{"facile":[{"type":"qcm","q":"You have a fever. You ___ see a doctor.","choices":["should","shouldn’t","mustn’t","don’t have to"],"answer":0,"explain":"Advice → should."},{"type":"direct","q":"Pain in the head is a ___.","accept":["headache"],"display":"headache","explain":"head + ache."},{"type":"qcm","q":"Modal verbs are followed by…","choices":["the base verb","to + verb","verb-ing","verb + -s"],"answer":0,"explain":"He should go (not “should to go”)."}],"moyen":[{"type":"qcm","q":"You ___ smoke in the hospital. It’s forbidden.","choices":["mustn’t","don’t have to","should","have to"],"answer":0,"explain":"Forbidden → mustn’t.","why":[null,"“Don’t have to” means it is not necessary, not forbidden.","“Should” gives advice to do it.","“Have to” is an obligation to do it."]},{"type":"direct","q":"Complete: “If I ___ you, I would rest.”","accept":["were"],"display":"were","explain":"Advice structure: If I were you, I would…"},{"type":"qcm","q":"Tomorrow is a holiday, so we ___ go to school.","choices":["don’t have to","mustn’t","must","should"],"answer":0,"explain":"No obligation → don’t have to."}],"difficile":[{"type":"qcm","q":"Find the mistake: “She musts to take her medicine twice a day.”","choices":["musts to take → must take","take → takes","twice → two","There is no mistake."],"answer":0,"explain":"Modals take no -s and no “to”."},{"type":"direct","q":"Rewrite with “should”: “It’s a good idea for you to sleep more.” → You ___ sleep more.","accept":["should"],"display":"should","explain":"A good idea = advice = should."},{"type":"qcm","q":"“Why don’t you ___ some exercise?”","choices":["do","to do","doing","did"],"answer":0,"explain":"“Why don’t you” + base verb."}]}}